<title>CANADA: Molson posts '97 profit after huge loss.</title>
<headline>Molson posts '97 profit after huge loss.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>fourth quarter ended March 31</p>
<p>				1997			    1996</p>
<p> Shr			    nil     loss	C$0.22</p>
<p> Net			    nil     loss	12,800</p>
<p> Revs		     303,000		  296,000</p>
<p>	   12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr	profit	 C$0.57     loss	C$5.27</p>
<p> Net	profit	 33,500     loss     305,500</p>
<p> Revs		   1,482,400		1,443,000</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>Full company name is Molson Cos Ltd.</p>
<p>NOTE: Fourth quarter and full-year 1997 results included a C$79.3 million charge related to the settlement of a licensing dispute with Adolph Coors Co. Ths was partly offset by a C$24 million gain on the sale of Molson's stake in Reno-Depot Inc  RD.M.</p>
<p>1996 results included C$270.2 million in losses from discontinued operations and C$103.5 million in charges for real estate losses and restructuring.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau 416 941-8100))</p>
